WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.202 --> 00:00:02.198
- Hi, I'm Amber Jay and we're here

00:00:02.198 --> 00:00:04.940
at BuzzFeed Motion Pictures
where people come from

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.573
across the country and, even
around the world, to work.

00:00:08.573 --> 00:00:10.744
And they all got their start somewhere

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.002
so I'm gonna go around the office and ask,

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:14.826
what was your first job?

00:00:14.826 --> 00:00:15.663
- My first job ...

00:00:15.663 --> 00:00:17.406
- My very first job ...

00:00:17.406 --> 00:00:19.662
- My first job was working at the Gap.

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:21.953
(crickets chirping)

00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:23.798
No one laughed.

00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:25.062
Okay, good, I feel good.

00:00:25.062 --> 00:00:28.033
- I opened my own lemonade
stand when I was 12

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:32.928
and I hired my brother and
my neighbors to work for me.

00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:35.429
- My parents were like,
you're gonna get a job at 14.

00:00:35.429 --> 00:00:37.263
- It was like a bookshop and cafe.

00:00:37.263 --> 00:00:39.783
15, I got a job doing that.

00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:42.196
Just making pizza, bagels and lattes.

00:00:42.196 --> 00:00:45.425
- 16 and I worked at McDonald's.

00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:47.831
- I was a cashier at a Chinese restaurant.

00:00:47.831 --> 00:00:50.801
- I worked for nuns and
I did their marketing.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.526
- Bath and Body Works.

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:53.839
- Camp counselor.

00:00:53.839 --> 00:00:55.881
- I sold knives for Cutco.

00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:59.338
- A summer internship at a tech company.

00:00:59.338 --> 00:01:02.553
- I was a host at Joe's Crab Shack.

00:01:02.553 --> 00:01:06.103
So I answered the phone, I
took people to their tables

00:01:06.103 --> 00:01:09.602
and I cleaned up the
bathroom of a Crab Shack.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.074
- You have to pick up all the popcorn,

00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:12.414
you have to sweep everything up.

00:01:12.414 --> 00:01:14.546
- Clean up the cafeteria
and all the hallways

00:01:14.546 --> 00:01:17.632
and the dorms and vacuum
and do stuff like that.

00:01:17.632 --> 00:01:19.587
It was a shitty job and I hated it.

00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:21.404
- Assistant pet groomer.

00:01:21.404 --> 00:01:23.640
- Being a PA on set, I
had to pick up dog poop

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.425
for a good couple weeks before I got paid.

00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:28.403
- Acting as an extra on a movie.

00:01:28.403 --> 00:01:30.228
- It was at a Korean
entertainment company.

00:01:30.228 --> 00:01:32.121
I started as an intern there.

00:01:32.121 --> 00:01:34.038
I made a lot of coffee.

00:01:39.879 --> 00:01:41.962
(laughs)

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:47.038
- I was making sandwiches
and now I can make

00:01:47.038 --> 00:01:49.245
a really good sandwich, not
just because I'm a woman.

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:50.635
- I used to answer the phone like this,

00:01:50.635 --> 00:01:52.941
welcome to ANA hardware where we put

00:01:52.941 --> 00:01:54.728
the word, hard, in hardware.

00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:57.612
(laughs)

00:01:57.612 --> 00:02:01.848
No lie, my boss was like, you
gotta cut that (bleep) out.

00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:05.733
My philosophy in life
is just take each day

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:08.902
one step at a time and just
don't worry about the future.

00:02:08.902 --> 00:02:10.500
- You should be able to find some amount

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.976
of happiness in what you're doing.

00:02:11.976 --> 00:02:15.798
- Don't think something's
out of reach or unattainable.

00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:17.680
- If you're pursuing an artistic career,

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.951
I think jobs are for quitting
and your career is your art.

00:02:20.951 --> 00:02:23.560
- You never know what opportunity
leads to your next one.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.666
So, it might seem like a shitty job,

00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:27.203
but doing that shitty job might help you

00:02:27.203 --> 00:02:29.329
meet a really cool person that
helps you get a better job.

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:30.746
- Get this paper.

00:02:32.987 --> 00:02:34.394
- Whatever you do, you do your best.

00:02:34.394 --> 00:02:36.763
Don't half-ass anything,
that's what I would say.

00:02:36.763 --> 00:02:38.641
If you gonna clean toilets, you gonna be

00:02:38.641 --> 00:02:41.058
the best toilet cleaner ever.

